    "agent_last_message": "Implemented in `/workspace/output/`:\n\n- [CMakeLists.txt](/workspace/output/CMakeLists.txt#L1) builds a C++20 `wordcount` executable.\n- [main.cpp](/workspace/output/main.cpp#L1) parses `--input` and `--output`, streams the input file in binary mode, counts lines/words/characters/unique words, computes the top 10 words with the required sort order, and writes valid JSON with escaping.\n\nBehavior matches the spec:\n- whitespace-separated words only\n- case-insensitive frequency counting via lowercase ASCII normalization\n- line counting based on `\\n`\n- `top_words` sorted by count descending, then lexicographically ascending\n- exit code `1` for invalid invocation or unreadable input\n- exit code `2` for unexpected/internal failures such as output write errors\n\nVerified build with:\n\n```bash\ncmake -B build && cmake --build build\n```\n\nand spot-checked the empty-file, trailing-newline, and tie-ordering cases."
